### 1. Task outcome (short version):
The 9-variable system's dynamics were identified as a set of coupled quadratic 
ordinary differential equations. The identification used finite differences 
(dt=0.001) for derivative estimation and least-squares regression on a library 
of linear and quadratic features. The model achieved a mean absolute residual of
0.149, suggesting a unimodal system. Significant residual spikes at indices 
1000, 11000, and 21000 correspond to the start of each data sample and likely 
indicate initial transients rather than mode transitions.

